.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-exec 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-exec \- Run a command, passing its streams and its exit code through unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten exec\fR [\fB\-\-capture\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-tee\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-style\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIcommand\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command, passing its streams and its exit code through unchanged
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-capture\-only\fR
Store the child\*(Aqs streams and report their handles instead of passing the bytes through
.TP
\fB\-\-tee\fR
Copy the child\*(Aqs streams onto Batten\*(Aqs own, as well as capturing them
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR [default: human]
How Batten\*(Aqs own record is encoded (hk\*(Aqs axis)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human: Pointer lines, one per fact
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON document
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: One JSON record per line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR [default: interleave]
How a teed child\*(Aqs bytes are presented, and whose output is suppressed (mise\*(Aqs axis)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
prefix: Each line carries the child\*(Aqs program name
.IP \(bu 2
interleave: The child\*(Aqs bytes, verbatim and as they arrive
.IP \(bu 2
keep\-order: Each stream whole, in a fixed order, after the child exits
.IP \(bu 2
replacing: As [`OutputStyle::Prefix`]: redrawing in place needs a terminal Batten never assumes it has
.IP \(bu 2
timed: As [`OutputStyle::Prefix`], minus the clock — see the type\*(Aqs docs
.IP \(bu 2
quiet: Batten says nothing of its own; the child still speaks
.IP \(bu 2
silent: Nobody speaks
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIcommand\fR>
The command to run, after `\-\-`, with its own arguments intact
